# Page Object Model Standards

## Locator Rules
- Store all selectors in a separate locator file.
- Use meaningful names.
- Avoid hardcoded selectors inside page classes.

Example:
```typescript
const HomePageLocators = {
    heroSection: '.elementor-widget-hero',
    navMenu: '#primary-menu',
    contactLink: 'a[href*="contact"]',
    servicesDropdown: '.menu-item-has-children'
}
export default HomePageLocators;
```

## Page Class Rules

- One class per one feature/page.
- Import locators.
- Methods should perform actions.
- Constructor takes `page: Page`.

Example structure:

```typescript
import { Page } from "@playwright/test";
import HomePageLocators from "../objectrepositories/HomePageLocators";

class HomePage {
  constructor(private readonly page: Page) {}

  get heroSection() {
    return this.page.locator(HomePageLocators.heroSection);
  }

  async navigateToContact() {
    await this.page.locator(HomePageLocators.contactLink).click();
  }

  async openServicesDropdown() {
    await this.page.locator(HomePageLocators.servicesDropdown).hover();
  }
}

export default HomePage;
```

## Do Not:
- Write page.locator() inside spec files.
- Duplicate locators across files.
- Add waits unless absolutely necessary.
